10.The cost of all of the above will be paid for by the City, WYDOT, and others
involved in the design and construction of thenewwork.
11.It is understood the City will pay the Courtiers the appraised value of this
renegotiated Memorandum of Agreement, also known among the parties as a lease, to use the
Courtiers’land fora detention pond to alleviate or solve the regional drainage problems, but in no
case will this amount be less than twenty-five thousand and no/100 dollars ($25,000.00).
In witness thereof, the Parties to this MOA, through their duly authorized representatives,
have executed this MOA on the days and dates set out below and certify that they have read,
